Z||000000||FieroFanaticus2||10-20-2001||03:02 PM||||A guy near me is selling an '84 white coupe.<BR>It has power windows and locks, a factory sunroof, and luggage racks.  On the entire car the only parts I want are the door (for the PW and PL) and the sunroof.  The rest of Everything is up for grabs or would be going on ebay.  He was asking $1250, but lowered the price to $750, and I talked him down to $475.  Here is what is wrong with the car.<P>1. Spiderweb cracks in the paint - no big deal.<BR>2.Radiator Damaged<BR>3.Driver's side door skin/panel cracked by mirror<BR>4. Both front wheel bearings are worn<BR>5. Drivers side door weather seal damaged.<BR>6. drivers side rear directional signal reflector cracked<BR>7. undercarriage severaly rusted<BR>8. missing side intake hose to air filter<BR>9. PCV Leaking badly<BR>10. Valve cover gasket is shot<BR>11. Oxygen sensor is broken in two<BR>12. oil on dipstick looks like chocolate milk<BR>13. drivers side interior door panel is peeling away from door -- probably just the fastners<BR>14. rust at the bottom left corner of drivers side door - not much, could be sanded off<BR>15. corners of dash severely busted - missing plastic, might be able to repair.<BR>16. heater/radio bezel detached, console warped.<BR>17. holes in headliner, headliner also falling<BR>18. seats badly torn<BR>19. seatbelt guides broken away from seats<BR>20. passenger side armrest is pulled away from door<BR>21. passenger inside door handle not functioning properly -- sticks a little<BR>22. high idle - 2150 rpm's, kicks down after about 10 minutes<BR>23. smokes on start up for about 5 minutes, smells bad -- worn valves?<BR>24. Cables to rear brakes are busted.<P>Some of that is just small stuff that really makes no difference.  Good points on the car are;<BR>1. All body panels seem intact, except the cracked door panel.<BR>2. Side panels (black plastic ones behind the doors) are PERFECT and shiny.<BR>3. Car started right up on first try<BR>4. BOTH headlight motors work<BR>5. Most interior parts are in good to excellent condition<BR>6. Power windows and locks work<BR>7. Speakers in headrests, could be reupholstered<BR>8. Still some good parts in the engine<P><BR>Do you think if I gave the guy $475 for it that I would be able to get aleast most of my money back by parting it out, basically to the bones?  <P>Anybody have any thoughts on this?  Oh, it's an automatic transmission.<P>Let me know what you think.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Monkeyman||10-20-2001||03:11 PM||||Personally, I wouldn't buy it.  I just gave away a non running '86 SC.  Very, very rough, but at least the frame wasn't rusty.  With a rusty frame, you'd have to part it out.  Not worth the time, effort or money to fix it if the rust is really bad.||||reg||1
